Saturday evening, Anitha comes to my flat.
She brings Tommy along too.
As soon as the door opens, Tommy runs inside happily.
I give him a small toy.
We sit near the dining table.
I serve the Mexican food I made in the afternoon.
Anitha tastes it and smiles.
"This is very tasty, Maya!" Anitha says.
"It is a little spicy, right?" I ask.
"No, this is perfect for us Malayalis," she says with a laugh.
We talk about this week's news.
I tell her about things at the office and the news from the cafe.
Outside the rain drums on, but inside the flat there is such warmth and happiness.
After the meal, Tommy sleeps near my feet.
In January, everything here was new to me.
Now I have friends and a good daily routine.
Kochi is no longer just a new city to me.
This is my own home.
